<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Corrected version of the 14-rule import file.

  What changed vs the original (and why each row was being rejected):
  - UnitSeconds/UnitCount/UnitKB were not recognised, so every SET_RATE lacked
    its required Unit. Replaced with <Unit> + <RatePerUnits>, the columns the
    importer maps ("0.50 per 60 SECOND").
  - PulseRounding / VolumeRounding / MatchStrategy / MaximumUnits /
    BundleRemaining(Operator) were unrecognised noise and are dropped.
    PulseSeconds is kept - it maps to SET_PULSE (60 means 60/60).
  - R007: BundleCode/BalanceType produced a broken DEDUCT_BALANCE with no
    amount source and no bundle action. Replaced with <Bundle>VOICE100</Bundle>,
    which maps to CONSUME_BUNDLE - the required action for a FREE_UNIT rule.
  - Catalogue entries this file references were created first:
    NIGHT time band, VOICE100 bundle, CORP500 offer, LOCAL and FRANCE zones.
-->
